evidence_text:
- AES-CBC encryption only pads plaintext to the next 32-byte boundary; ciphertext/base64 length therefore varies with plaintext length (no constant-size padding): [
  /workdir/repo/bank.py:38-58
].
- Bank returns different JSON structures on success vs failure: for create (mode "n") it includes a "card" field; for balance (mode "g") it includes a "balance" field; on any exception it returns only {"code":1}. This makes success/failure and (for balance) the numeric string length distinguishable via message length: [
  /workdir/repo/bank.py:171-224
].
- Bank sends the (variable-length) JSON response over the network after encryption; on protocol exceptions it closes without sending a response (connection-level metadata difference): [
  /workdir/repo/bank.py:303-326
].
- No protection of connection metadata: bank binds a normal TCP server socket on localhost: [
  /workdir/repo/bank.py:335-347
].
- ATM request size depends on the operation JSON, which includes the (variable-length) account name, then encrypts and sends it directly over TCP (leaking account name length via ciphertext length): [
  /workdir/repo/atm.py:240-264
  /workdir/repo/atm.py:294-311
].
